# ============================================================================
# .dev.vars.example — template for local development only
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file:
#         cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#   2. Fill in real local-only values (if any).
#   3. NEVER commit .dev.vars — it is git-ignored.
#
# HOW IT WORKS
#   `wrangler dev` reads .dev.vars and exposes each key on `env` inside the
#   Worker, exactly like Cloudflare Worker Secrets do in production.
#
# SECURITY RULES
#   • This file (*.example) is a TEMPLATE. It must contain no real keys.
#   • Do NOT paste production credentials here. If you need a real key for
#     testing, request a separate sandbox key from the provider.
#   • Anything in `.dev.vars` stays on your machine. Wrangler never uploads it.
#   • The repository is PUBLIC. Assume every committed byte is world-readable.
# ============================================================================


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-secret runtime configuration (safe to edit freely)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allowed values: "development" | "production"
ENVIRONMENT=development

# Comma-separated list of browser origins allowed by CORS.
# When omitted, src/config.ts falls back to DEFAULT_ALLOWED_ORIGINS
# (GitHub Pages + common localhost ports).
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8787,http://127.0.0.1:8787,http://localhost:5500,http://127.0.0.1:5500,https://surajsrkoli-gif.github.io


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FUTURE SECRETS — PHASE 3+
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The keys below are declared in src/types.ts as optional strings so the code
# is ready for them. They are NOT read anywhere in Phase 2 and MUST remain
# commented out until the corresponding phase begins.
#
# When Phase 3 starts, uncomment a line and paste a SANDBOX / FREE-TIER key
# here for local testing only. For production, use:
#
#     wrangler secret put MARKET_DATA_API_KEY
#     wrangler secret put NEWS_API_KEY
#     wrangler secret put AI_API_KEY
#
# Each `wrangler secret put` command prompts for the value and stores it
# encrypted in Cloudflare. Nothing is written to disk or committed to GitHub.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Phase 3 — real market data provider(s)
# MARKET_DATA_API_KEY=replace-with-sandbox-key

# Phase 4/5 — news and sentiment feed
# NEWS_API_KEY=replace-with-sandbox-key

# Phase 6 — AI analysis engine
# AI_API_KEY=replace-with-sandbox-key


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — local overrides for debugging
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to "1" to enable verbose request logging inside the Worker.
# The handler would read this via env.DEBUG and print structured logs that
# `wrangler tail` can display. Not wired up in Phase 2.
# DEBUG=0
